## Risk Assessment {#risk-assessment}

### High Risks (If fixes not applied) {#high-risks-if-fixes-not-applied}

```
🔴 CRITICAL RISKS
├─ Account takeover via brute-force (rate limiter)
├─ Session hijacking (no logout revocation)
├─ Unauthorized API access (no middleware)
└─ PII exposure via OOM crash (memory leak)

Impact: Data breach, compliance violation, incident response cost
Likelihood: HIGH (common attack patterns)
Timeline: Could happen within first week of production
```

### Medium Risks (If Phase 2 deferred) {#medium-risks-if-phase-2-deferred}

```
🟠 MEDIUM RISKS
├─ Difficult incident debugging (no tracing)
├─ Admin password never expires
├─ TOTP migration issues
└─ Performance degradation under load (memory leak)

Impact: Slow incident response, compliance questions
Likelihood: MEDIUM (would surface within 2 weeks)
Timeline: Production issues within 30 days
```

### Low Risks (If Phase 3 deferred) {#low-risks-if-phase-3-deferred}

```
🟡 LOW RISKS
├─ Email enumeration timing attacks
├─ Missing CORS headers
└─ Password change spam

Impact: Minor security/UX issues
Likelihood: LOW (require specific attacker knowledge)
Timeline: Non-urgent improvements
```

